    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18099" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fictūra</span></b> , ae, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				forming</i>, <i>fashioning</i> (ante- and
			post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fortunae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Trin. 2, 2, 86</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">satis placet fictura,</span>”
				i. e. <i>disguise</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Mil. 4, 4, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">avarus ab uno solum verbo inclinatum, quod est
					aveo eademque fictura, qua est amarus,</span>”
				<i>formation</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					10, 5, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
